<title>PORTUGAL: Aramco, Petrogal to end talks by early '97 - paper.</title>
<headline>Aramco, Petrogal to end talks by early '97 - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>A senior Portuguese official was quoted as saying that talks between state oil firm Petrogal and Saudi Aramco with a view to Aramco taking a stake in Petrogal were expected to be concluded by early 1997 at the latest.</p>
<p>&quot;The talks with Saudi Aramco will be concluded by the end of this year or early next year,&quot; Under-Secretary for Finance Fernando Teixeira dos Santos told Diario de Noticias newspaper in an interview.</p>
<p>Under-Secretary for Industry and Energy Jose Penedos told Reuters last month that Saudi Aramco could take a stake of up to 35 percent in Petrogal-Petroleos de Portugal.</p>
<p>-- David Brough, Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
